  "database": "rschema_0333",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0333 database is designed to manage user information and their interactions on a social networking platform. The User table stores information about each user, including their address, birthday, current location, email, gender, hometown, interests, motto, name, password, personal profile, phone number, relationship status, user type, and username. The User_ID is the primary key, uniquely identifying each user, and is a required field. The User_homepage table represents a user's homepage, containing details such as creation time, title, and introduction, with a foreign key referencing the User table to link the homepage to its owner. The User_connection_request_record table tracks user connection requests, including the sender and receiver's user IDs, the send time, and a unique record ID. The User_connection_establishment_record table records established connections between users, with foreign keys referencing the User table to identify the sender and receiver. The Feed table stores user posts, including the feed content, post time, and a foreign key referencing the User table to identify the poster and the User_homepage table to identify the homepage where the post was made. The User_homepage_join table tracks when a user joins a homepage, with a composite primary key of join time, homepage ID, and user ID, and foreign keys referencing the User_homepage and User tables to link the join to the homepage and user.",
  "gold_question": "Description of Social Network System Requirements: For user registration and login, users can register and log in to the system using username and password. The system supports different types of users, such as regular users and administrators. For personal information management, users can fill in and manage basic personal information, including name, phone, address, email, birthday, gender, relationship status, interests, etc., and can edit detailed information such as personal profile, motto, hometown, and current location. For user connection management, users can establish connections with other users, and the system records the connection time. Users can send and receive connection requests, and the system records the request sending time. For user homepage management, users can create personal homepages, including title, introduction, and creation time. Other users can join user's homepage and the joining time is recorded. For homepage feed management, users can post updates on their own homepage, including text content, and the posting time is recorded. Other users can also post updates on user's homepage, creating interaction. For the functionality of users joining multiple homepages, users can join multiple different homepages, and the joining time is recorded. The system supports associations between users and multiple homepages.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0333.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0333\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birthday` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hometown` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `current_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `interests` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `motto` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `relationship_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_homepage` (\n  `homepage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`homepage_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_homepage_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_connection_request_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sender_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `send_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_connection_establishment_record` (\n  `establishment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sender_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`establishment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_establishment_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_establishment_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `feed` (\n  `feed_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `homepage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `post_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`feed_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `feed_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `feed_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`homepage_id`) REFERENCES `user_homepage` (`homepage_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_homepage_join` (\n  `join_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `homepage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`join_time`, `homepage_id`, `user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_homepage_join_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`homepage_id`) REFERENCES `user_homepage` (`homepage_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_homepage_join_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
